t discard: Choose among single tiles that are less dangerous (not giving others pung/kong). Given other players\u2019 histories: Next player has W7 W8 W9 chow, so may need W5 W6 or W4? Possibly dangerous to discard W4 if they are collecting Wan suit. Previous player\u2019s history shows many honors discards (F3, F1, F4, F2, J1, J2, J3) \u2014 they seem to be discarding honors, so less likely to need F tiles.  \n\nDiscard W4 is safe (only 3 W8, 3 W9, 4 W4 unshown \u2014 but no indication they are collecting Wan except next player\u2019s single chow). Alternatively discard W2 is similar.  \n\nBut note: My hand has many pairs, so I should keep pairs for pung opportunities. Singles W4 and W2 are less useful. I should discard one of them. W4 is slightly more connected to W5 W6 but I have none. W2 can form chow with W1 W3 but I have none.  \n\nChoice: Discard W4 to keep W2? W2 has slightly more tiles left (4 unshown) than W4 (4 unshown) so equal. I'll discard W4.  \n\nReason:  \nI choose to discard W4 because it\u2019s a single tile with no immediate pairing or sequencing potential in my hand, while retaining all pairs (F4, T6, B6) for potential pungs, and keeping singles W2, T1, F1 as possible draws to match for new pairs. This maximizes pung chances for a quick hand completion toward Chicken Hand (8 points) or possibly All Pungs (6) combined with other small patterns to reach 8+ points.  \n\nAnswer: Play W4"}
